.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt NODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm node ,
.Nm npm ,
.Nm npx
.Nd run JavaScript and manage its packages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm node
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar script Op Ar argument ...
.Nm npm
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm npx
.Op Ar options
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm node
runs JavaScript with the V8 engine.
With no script it starts an interactive interpreter;
.Fl e Ar source
runs source given on the command line.
.Nm npm
installs and manages packages from the npm registry or local files.
.Nm npx
runs a package's command, downloading it when it is absent.
.Ql node --help ,
.Ql npm help
and
.Ql npx --help
list their options and commands.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root includes the official Node.js 26.13.0 LTS build with
npm and npx 11.20.0 when built with
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=node
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all .
The archive is installed under
.Pa /opt/node ;
.Pa /usr/bin
and
.Pa /bin
have links to its three commands.
Node uses the GNU root's glibc and GCC's C++ and atomic runtime libraries.
Its MIT license and bundled notices are in
.Pa /opt/node/LICENSE ;
npm's Artistic License 2.0 and dependency notices are in
.Pa /opt/node/lib/node_modules/npm/LICENSE .
.Pp
An install without
.Fl g
writes packages under the current project's
.Pa node_modules .
A global install needs write access to npm's prefix;
.Ql npm config set prefix ~/.local
chooses a prefix in the user's home.
Add that prefix's
.Pa bin
to
.Ev PATH
to run its commands.
Package installs and npx may run scripts supplied by those packages.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.npmrc
npm's user settings
.It Pa ~/.npm
npm's default cache and logs
.It Pa package.json
project metadata and dependencies
.It Pa package-lock.json
versions resolved by npm
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ node -e 'console.log("hello")'
$ npm install --prefix ./project ./package.tgz
$ npx --no -- node --version
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1
.Pp
.Lk https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v26.x/api/ "The Node.js API"
.Lk https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/ "The npm manual"
